@flexiarg meta/observe-the-meta-field
@title Observe the META Field Before Filling a Policy
@sigils [👓/见]
@keywords META, outer loop, observation, mission, excursion, ticket, algorithm, injury, interoception, policy
@audience War Machine designers, pattern-policy constructors, operators
@tone operational-analytic
@references [meta/exotype-determines-behaviour cascades/on-the-fly-cascade]
@status [status[ready] "evidence[2026-10-02 debugger run selected completed and unreasoned excursions; E-outer-loop-improvement]"]

! conclusion:
  Observe the complete M/E/T/A field and the machine's own condition before
  constructing outer-policy candidates, so policy slots are filled from the
  current world rather than from a fixed task list.

  + context: The War Machine is about to choose what kind of work to do next.

  + IF:
    Missions, excursions, tickets, and approved algorithms are possible next
    acts, while runtime evidence may also say that the machine is injured.

  + HOWEVER:
    A flat enumeration says what exists but not which branch of policy space is
    currently viable. Ignoring interoception makes ordinary work compete with
    self-repair even when the machine cannot safely perform it.

  + THEN:
    Produce one source-pinned observation containing the complete M/E/T/A
    census, typed exclusions, task-level evidence, resource state, recent
    outcomes, and typed injury observations. Absence of injury evidence is an
    explicit absence, never a healthy default.

  + BECAUSE:
    Active inference selects under a generative model of the current state.
    The candidate policy family cannot be correct if the state observation
    omits either available work or the machine's capacity to enact it.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Feed this observation into typed META policy slots without consulting tactical cascades or G from the inner loop.]
